PS4 OS Builder - the PS4 Linux build with the distribution left out.

The scripts and documentation in this repository are MIT (see LICENSE).

They fetch, and are meant to be used with, other people's work:

  app/ (the installer)         OpenOrbis PS4 Toolchain, GPL-3.0. A copy of the
                               app published in
                               github.com/shanerm420/ps4-linux-desktop, kept in
                               this repository so this project stands alone
  kernel (boot/bzImage)        Linux, GPL-2.0, from gitlab.com/rmuxnet/linux
                               branch ps4/7.3.4; sources at
                               github.com/shanerm420/ps4-linux-kernel
  initramfs (boot/)            built from feeRnt/ps4-linux-initramfs (BSD-3)
                               with the GPL-3.0 boot function
  Mesa patch                   MIT (the patch is published with the Mesa it
                               patches)

Your distribution is yours: it keeps its own licences, and they are your problem
and your responsibility. Two things not to do:

  * do not bundle Sony-extracted blobs - liverpool_*.bin, gladius_*.bin, the EAP
    HDD key. The loader takes those from OrbisOS memory at boot, which is what
    keeps any of this distributable;
  * do not redistribute a distribution whose licence forbids it (ChromeOS Flex is
    the obvious example).

Nothing here is supported by Sony. A jailbroken console can always be left in a
state that needs recovery.
